# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# V2 fixture harness JS deps (fixtures.json itself is committed).
# The lockfile IS committed: the fixtures are byte-exact expectations produced by yjs+lib0,
# so the exact transitive versions are part of the expectation.
v2_test_fixtures/node_modules

# Cross-impl fuzz harness JS deps (NDJSON cases are generated on demand).
# The lockfile IS committed — it is what actually pins the oracle's reference side. yjs@13.6.31
# depends on `lib0: ^0.2.99`, and lib0 is the encoder every byte-exact comparison is made
# against; without the lockfile each CI run resolved a different lib0 (0.2.117 locally, 18
# patches past the floor), so the oracle's ground truth could drift between runs.
fuzz/node_modules


# Rust benchmark harness build output (bench/yrs is a comparison harness, not a dependency)
bench/yrs/target/

# ygo benchmark harness build output (bench/ygo is a comparison harness, not a dependency)
bench/ygo/ygo-bench

# Generated benchmark output. status.html is regenerated by bench/status.py from the raw harness
# files beside it; committing either would let a stale page outlive the numbers it reports.
bench-results/
bench/__pycache__/
bench-results-amd64/
